TI  - NITROGENOUS EXCRETION BY MEIOFAUNA FROM CORAL-REEF SEDIMENTS - MECOR-5
T2  - MARINE BIOLOGY
LA  - English
AB  - Nitrogenous excretion rates of meiofauna from coral sediments of the Great Barrier Reef, Australia were studied at winter temperatures. Data on single taxa fitted a geometric regression: Log N excretion=-0.206+0.865 log x where log x=dry weight in .mu.g. Abundance and biomass data on meiofaunal taxa were obtained from Lizard Island, Orpheus Island and Davies Reef. Using excretion rates and biomass data, meiofauna were calculated as contributing 10.18, 12.32, and 1.60 mg N m-2 h-1 at the above areas, respectively.
